  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Prompt\'s Specs**\n\nI\'m deep in the prompt\'s details now. Focusing on \"Ruang Karakter\" and the Android app (Kotlin + Jetpack Compose) for MRI learning. I\'m carefully reading the specifications to pinpoint the core requirements for this new feature.\n\n\n**Defining the Character Space**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Character Space\". The goal is clear: allow users to edit their avatar within a dedicated space, which visually integrates with the Home screen\'s MRI control room theme. Key components include progress-based unlockable customizations, ensuring the avatar feels like it\'s *in situ* the MRI control room. The MVVM architecture and the provided UI elements are useful.\n\n\n**Refining UI Component Specs**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of UI components. The \"Character Space\" demands a glowing stage design, category tabs (Hair, Uniform, Headset, Background), grid items with color options, and \"Reset\" / \"Save & Return\" buttons. It\'s time to check the tab navigation requirements.\n\n\n**Mapping Data Models & Flow**\n\nI\'m now outlining data models: hair, uniform, headset, background are key. I\'m focusing on `customColorHex`, `latarId`, and ensuring compatibility with the old `userAvatarId`. I\'m devising unlock rules based on data, not hardcoded UI elements. Curriculum progress (using existing data like `completedCount` and `completedNodeCodes`) will determine locked/unlocked states. Reset button functionality and DataStore interaction for \"Save & Return\" are being finalized, with updates reflecting immediately on the home screen.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_5495493919668029391"
