  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the New Card**\n\nI\'m focusing on the updated `HeroProgressCard`, visualizing it as the MRI Control Room scene. The aesthetic is taking shape: a deep navy and obsidian gradient background, complete with a scanner window and a red digital clock header. I\'m aiming for a visually striking and thematic design.\n\n\n**Refining the Card Structure**\n\nI\'m now integrating the avatar display and Ruang Karakter button into the console design, which is in front of a console table. I\'ve designed the \"progres pemindaian\" monitors, with the initial state in grey, changing to cyan/emerald on progress. The \"Lanjutkan\" button is set at the bottom. I\'m focusing on the implementation details now. I\'m working on the `HeroProgressCard` implementation based on the `HomeScreen` call.\n\n\n**Implementing the New Design**\n\nI\'m now incorporating the proposed layout. I\'ve placed the user avatar and name, along with the \"Ruang Karakter\" button, at the top. The \"progres pemindaian\" monitors will be visualized below, reflecting scanning progress. I am developing the initial grey state, and its progress-based color changes to cyan and emerald. The \"Lanjutkan\" button will be positioned at the bottom, per the structure. I\'m focusing on the component\'s implementation.\n\n\n**Adding Control Room Details**\n\nI\'ve added the MRI suite time/location label in a box, framed with a warning color. I\'ve also incorporated the \"Ruang Karakter\" button, styled as a clickable surface with its own cyan aesthetic. It\'s designed to align with the console table\'s look. Now I am planning the integration of this information to complete the scanner window display.\n\n\n**Constructing the Scan Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the scan progress visualization within the card. I\'ve built the row containing the user\'s avatar, and am now incorporating the three scan progress monitors. Each monitor will display the progress of a specific learning module with corresponding labels and progress bars. The logic for calculating the progress based on completed and total counts is being implemented. I\'m also ensuring the avatar click navigates to the character room. The button is being built.\n\n\n"
