  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Runtime Error**\n\nI\'m currently focused on a runtime error specifically related to `IllegalArgumentException` in the context of `MutableState` and `CharacterCustomizationState`. The core problem seems to be the saveable state registry\'s limitations regarding the character state. I\'m investigating how to best adapt the state for persistence or explore alternative saving mechanisms to overcome this restriction.\n\n\n**Implementing a Custom Saver**\n\nI\'ve decided to implement a custom `Saver` for `CharacterCustomizationState`, and pass it as a `stateSaver` parameter to `rememberSaveable()`. This approach is looking promising. The `CharacterCustomizationState` class\'s non-serializable nature was the source of the `IllegalArgumentException` during state saving.\n\n\n"
