  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Revising Hero Card Design**\n\nI\'m focusing on restoring the `HeroProgressCard` to its pristine layout. I\'ve decided to use `R.drawable.mri_scanner_hero` as the background, complete with a gradient overlay. The text will showcase \"PROGRES KURIKULUM KLINIS\" and display the competency node progress: \"$completedCount dari $totalCount\". A `LinearProgressIndicator` and a \"Lanjutkan\" pill will complete the design.\n\n\n**Refining Hero Card Layout**\n\nI\'ve restored the original `HeroProgressCard` design, omitting the \"Ruang Karakter\" button and custom progress visuals, as requested. The \"Karakter\" tab in the bottom navigation will now lead to `CharacterRoomScreen`. I\'ve checked the original implementation using a `Card` with a background image, text, a `LinearProgressIndicator`, and a \"Lanjutkan\" button. The layout is ready to be restored to its original implementation with an mri scanner image as background, and gradient.\n\n\n**Implementing Gradient Overlay**\n\nI\'ve added a gradient overlay to enhance text readability on the hero card. This overlay uses a vertical gradient from a dark transparent color to a slightly less transparent one, creating a visual distinction. Inside, I\'m organizing content with a column. It will show the clinical curriculum progress and display completed competency nodes, with a gradient-tinted background. I\'m focusing on text styling for better visibility against the background.\n\n\n**Finalizing Visual Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now integrating the progress indicator and \"Lanjutkan\" pill button within the `HeroProgressCard` design. A `LinearProgressIndicator` displays the progress using a calculated ratio. The \"Lanjutkan\" button, a `Surface` with a rounded shape, is designed to be clickable. I\'ve focused on styling, including the button\'s background and padding to achieve the desired look.\n\n\n"
